  "scope": "Simplify binary carry boundary arguments",
  "validation": "Paired target, ArithmeticRankForcing and ArithmeticSaturation builds pass with identical client objects. All 14 target declaration/type/axiom reports, 28,971 default simp entries and 13,167 instances match. The direct BinaryPopulation source/object pair matches a prior successful receipt.",
  "limitations": [
    "ArithmeticWindowDigits is another direct source client and was not rebuilt. Existing target linter warnings occur in both phases.",
    "The prior BinaryPopulation receipt does not pin its direct Foundation/Mathlib dependencies. Other project and package inputs remain cached; no complete current-source closure rebuild is established.",
    "An initial provisional setup failed because an empty overlay hid the Population provider; its log was overwritten by the later successful provisional run. That failure is described but its lost output cannot be independently checked.",
    "One paired shared-load timing sample does not establish a general performance effect. Probes cover the target object and the explicitly enumerated environment entries, not every persistent extension.",
    "The archive omits compiled objects; recorded object hashes are receipt claims and need the original external objects for independent byte checking."
  ],
